{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xca2aewJNUA9anF3MEheCT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t+++\n2\tid = \"WI-538\"\n3\ttitle = \"Arm the complexity sensor here at the ruled scope, and re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, 1c)\"\n4\tspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired\"\n5\tworkstream = \"process\"\n6\tsr_refs = []\n7\tneeds = [\"WI-537\", \"~WI-521\"]\n8\tbuildtier = \"medium\"\n9\tsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\n10\tpriority = 2\n11\t+++\n12\t\n13\t## Context\n14\t\n15\t**What this row does.** Phase 2 of the OI-68 complexity-sensor program, at the\n16\tshape the owner RULED on 2026-08-30 — **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a** (the record is\n17\t`docs/requirements/open-items.toml` `[open_item.OI-68]`, `status = \"ruled\"`). The\n18\tdriver recommended 1a (retire the line ratchet); the owner ruled **1c** — BOTH\n19\tsensors stay armed, they measure different axes (module SIZE and function\n20\tCOMPLEXITY), and the module-size ratchet is RE-BASED from raw physical lines to\n21\tSLOC. So this phase is **arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: nothing is deleted,\n22\tno pointer is moved. The plan's phase-2 draft\n23\t(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired`)\n24\tpredates the ruling and is written for 1a; the ruling governs where they differ.\n25\t\n26\t**Three acts, one direction.**\n27\t\n28\t1. **Arm (Q3 → 3a).** Add `[step:complexity]` to `docs/stack.ini`\n29\t   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) running\n30\t   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare in\n31\t   both directions, nonzero on either. Growth fails (\"simplify, or take a reviewed\n32\t   baseline bump whose reason lands in the log\"); improvement fails (\"re-stamp\n33\t   downward in the same commit\"). No inline suppression pragma — the central\n34\t   baseline is the one escape hatch. Arming mints NO new spine row: `SR-183`\n35\t   already carries both postures in one contract (\"gated only where a repo opts\n36\t   in\"), and the opt-in IS the step's presence here. Report-only stays the shipped\n37\t   default; shipping downstream is phase 3, a separate WI.\n38\t\n39\t2. **Scope (Q2 → 2a).** The sensor censuses `tests/` as well as\n40\t   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — widened in `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE`,\n41\t   the single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline`\n42\t   is re-stamped to seed the `tests/` functions over threshold. The line ratchet\n43\t   stays scripts-only, per the ruling. This closes WI-521's §3 sensor gap on the\n44\t   right axis instead of by extending the disputed line axis to a second tree.\n45\t\n46\t3. **Re-base (Q1 → 1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` re-bases from raw\n47\t   physical lines to **SLOC** (non-blank, non-comment, non-docstring) — the\n48\t   definition held once beside the sensor (`check_complexity.module_sloc`) and\n49\t   IMPORTED by the ratchet, so both sensors share one definition of a source line.\n50\t   `THRESHOLD` re-bases 1500 → **1000 SLOC**; the `BASELINE` dict is fully\n51\t   re-stamped to SLOC values with the derivation on record. Nothing deleted: the\n52\t   test file, its `docs/stack.ini` `[generated]` `linecounts` row, its\n53\t   `tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py` `OTHERWISE_ENFORCED` entry, and\n54\t   WI-521's debt-owner pointer all stay. WI-521's §3 is amended to record what the\n55\t   ruling answered (the sensor gap is now closed; the line ratchet keeps its\n56\t   distinct module-SIZE job on the code axis).\n57\t\n58\t**Threshold derivation.** The 9 modules the raw-1500 ratchet baselined score\n59\t1081–3364 SLOC (`intake.py` smallest at 1081); the largest non-member is\n60\t`traj_panels.py` at 891 SLOC. A SLOC threshold in 900–1000 preserves exactly those\n61\t9 — a clean 190-line gap — so 1000 re-stamps the current watch set onto the code\n62\taxis, deleting no entry and admitting none. That is the \"full re-stamp with the\n63\tderivation on record\" the ruling names.\n64\t\n65\t**Q4 → 4a** is already satisfied by the shipped sensor (match = one increment,\n66\tcomprehension `if` takes the nesting increment, threshold 15); nothing here\n67\tre-opens it.\n68\t\n69\t**Not in scope.** Retiring any sensor (ruled out by 1c). Shipping downstream (the\n70\t`bootstrap.MAPPING` row, the commented template step, the `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md`\n71\tlayer, the `deep-module-design` skill — all phase 3). The relative-churn sensor.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"790c25a0-4379-4c87-969a-fce808315ac0","uuid":"4030175b-e100-46a9-a87e-c70192c7de07","timestamp":"2026-08-31T02:55:36.898Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-drive\\wi-538-arm-and-rebase\\docs\\work\\active\\wi-538-arm-and-rebase\\WI-538-arm-and-rebase.md","content":"+++\nid = \"WI-538\"\ntitle = \"Arm the complexity sensor here at the ruled scope, and re-base the module-size ratchet to SLOC (OI-68 phase 2, 1c)\"\nspecref = \"docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired\"\nworkstream = \"process\"\nsr_refs = []\nneeds = [\"WI-537\", \"~WI-521\"]\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\npriority = 2\n+++\n\n## Context\n\n**What this row does.** Phase 2 of the OI-68 complexity-sensor program, at the\nshape the owner RULED on 2026-08-30 — **1c / 2a / 3a / 4a** (the record is\n`docs/requirements/open-items.toml` `[open_item.OI-68]`, `status = \"ruled\"`). The\ndriver recommended 1a (retire the line ratchet); the owner ruled **1c** — BOTH\nsensors stay armed, they measure different axes (module SIZE and function\nCOMPLEXITY), and the module-size ratchet is RE-BASED from raw physical lines to\nSLOC. So this phase is **arm + re-base**, never arm + retire: nothing is deleted,\nno pointer is moved. The plan's phase-2 draft\n(`docs/plans/2026-08-29-complexity-sensor-plan.md#phase-2--arm-it-here-and-retire-whichever-sensor-the-ruling-retired`)\npredates the ruling and is written for 1a; the ruling governs where they differ.\n\n**Three acts, one direction.**\n\n1. **Arm (Q3 → 3a).** Add `[step:complexity]` to `docs/stack.ini`\n   (`layer = product`, `from-stage = DevStg-Impl`) running\n   `check_complexity.py --root . --mode enforce` — the exact-equality compare in\n   both directions, nonzero on either. Growth fails (\"simplify, or take a reviewed\n   baseline bump whose reason lands in the log\"); improvement fails (\"re-stamp\n   downward in the same commit\"). No inline suppression pragma — the central\n   baseline is the one escape hatch. Arming mints NO new spine row: `SR-183`\n   already carries both postures in one contract (\"gated only where a repo opts\n   in\"), and the opt-in IS the step's presence here. Report-only stays the shipped\n   default; shipping downstream is phase 3, a separate WI.\n\n2. **Scope (Q2 → 2a).** The sensor censuses `tests/` as well as\n   `project-trajectory/scripts/` — widened in `check_complexity.DEFAULT_INCLUDE`,\n   the single home of this repo's census surface — and `docs/complexity-baseline`\n   is re-stamped to seed the `tests/` functions over threshold. The line ratchet\n   stays scripts-only, per the ruling. This closes WI-521's §3 sensor gap on the\n   right axis instead of by extending the disputed line axis to a second tree.\n\n3. **Re-base (Q1 → 1c).** `tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py` re-bases from raw\n   physical lines to **SLOC** (non-blank, non-comment, non-docstring) — the\n   definition held once beside the sensor (`check_complexity.module_sloc`) and\n   IMPORTED by the ratchet, so both sensors share one definition of a source line.\n   `THRESHOLD` re-bases 1500 → **1000 SLOC**; the `BASELINE` dict is fully\n   re-stamped to SLOC values with the derivation on record. Nothing deleted: the\n   test file, its `docs/stack.ini` `[generated]` `linecounts` row, its\n   `tests/test_generated_freshness_wiring.py` `OTHERWISE_ENFORCED` entry, and\n   WI-521's debt-owner pointer all stay. WI-521's §3 is amended to record what the\n   ruling answered (the sensor gap is now closed; the line ratchet keeps its\n   distinct module-SIZE job on the code axis).\n\n**Threshold derivation.** The 9 modules the raw-1500 ratchet baselined score\n1081–3364 SLOC (`intake.py` smallest at 1081); the largest non-member is\n`traj_panels.py` at 891 SLOC. A SLOC threshold in 900–1000 preserves exactly those\n9 — a clean 190-line gap — so 1000 re-stamps the current watch set onto the code\naxis, deleting no entry and admitting none. That is the \"full re-stamp with the\nderivation on record\" the ruling names.\n\n**Q4 → 4a** is already satisfied by the shipped sensor (match = one increment,\ncomprehension `if` takes the nesting increment, threshold 15); nothing here\nre-opens it.\n\n**Not in scope.** Retiring any sensor (ruled out by 1c). Shipping downstream (the\n`bootstrap.MAPPING` row, the commented template step, the `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md`\nlayer, the `deep-module-design` skill — all phase 3). The relative-churn sensor.\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
